WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.649
If you're like me, you're not

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.239
watching the Olympics, currently

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.709
taking place in that winter

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.689
wonderland of Beijing, China,

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.669
where the snow is totally fake, but

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.829
the silencing of American athletes

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.119
is depressingly real.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.619
The TV audience for the opening

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.449
ceremonies was down 43

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.429
percent compared to the last Winter

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.349
Games, and it's not just because

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.089
of yet another hideously ugly

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.279
mascot, time zone differences,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.379
and the cultural genocide of Uyghurs

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.369
killing the buzz.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.779
Olympics viewership has been

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.609
dropping for decades now, which is

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.409
a welcome development if you care

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.179
about human dignity and wasteful

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.169
government spending.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.119
The games are a global drift, run

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.979
by one of the most corrupt, scandal

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.629
ridden bodies in sports history.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.609
The International Olympic Committee

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.469
is happy to massively rip

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.449
off whatever sucker cities

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.309
and countries are dumb enough to

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.259
beg for the right to host that, I'm

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.019
looking at you, Los Angeles 2028.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.059
Like vampires, they suck their host

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.949
dry while providing legitimacy

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.809
to tyrants and monsters such as

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.729
Adolf Hitler, Leonid Brezhnev,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.279
Vladimir Putin and Xi Jinping.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.869
More important, they are the

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.639
embodiment of a worn out

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.469
collectivist, 20th century

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.119
attitude toward competition among

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.339
nations that makes no sense

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.169
in our increasingly globalized,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.669
individualistic world.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.369
The modern games got started in 1896

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.049
by French aristocrat Pierre de

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.569
Coubertin as a way of reviving

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.429
Gallic national pride after his

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.109
country got its ass kicked by

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.179
Germany in the Franco-Prussian War.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.679
That's why athletes represent

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.929
countries rather than themselves.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.669
And it's also why the Olympics were

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.409
politically charged to the hilt

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.449
throughout the 20th century, such

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.309
as in the 1936 Berlin

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.169
Games, which Hitler overtly

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.449
staged as a showcase for rising

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.639
German military might and aggression

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.629
during the Cold War.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.609
The Olympics functioned as one more

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.319
proxy battle in the twilight

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.179
struggle between the free world and

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.769
communism, when the U.S.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.269
and Soviet teams faced off in

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.679
basketball and hockey.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.299
It was every bit as much a

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.919
geopolitical showdown between

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.749
superpowers as anything

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.309
happening in Southeast Asia or

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.959
Central America that made the

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.939
Olympics more exciting to watch.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.949
Bruce Jenner kicking commie ass

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.559
in his world record setting 1976

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.449
decathlon victory wasn't just

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.069
about surpassing the limits of the

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:14.969
human body.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.219
It was somehow about realpolitik

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.359
in nuclear war.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.889
But there was a ton of collateral

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.539
damage from such a framing, with

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.309
ongoing national boycotts over

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.959
political disputes, meaning that

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.789
athletes would train for years

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.649
were figuratively sacrificed on the

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.479
altar of nationalism or as

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.339
in the case of murdered Israeli

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.499
athletes at the 1972 Munich

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.749
Games, literally killed in the name

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.459
of international politics.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.379
De Coubertin famously said that

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.059
the most important thing in the

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.039
Olympic Games is not to win, but

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:44.969
to take part.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.769
But when the Games are taking place

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.569
in an authoritarian country and

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.489
we're still tallying medals by

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.439
nation and the athletes are treated

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.479
like geopolitical pawns rather

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.279
than superlative individuals, it

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.289
makes more sense than ever to tune

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.609
out the Olympics.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.049
Let the competitors represent

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.939
themselves on a neutral playing

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.799
field far from the distraction of

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.539
politics, and you'll see the

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.429
audience return ready to cheer

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.799
athletes who inspire us by embodying

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.319
the Olympic ideal of going faster,

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.460
higher, stronger.

